<article class="env-definition" id="09EC">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/09EC">Definition <span data-tag="09EC">15.114.3</span>.</a> Let $A$ be a discrete valuation ring with fraction field $K$. Let $L/K$ be a finite Galois extension with Galois group $G$. Let $B$ be the integral closure of $A$ in $L$. Let $\mathfrak m \subset B$ be a maximal ideal. </p>
  <p><ol>
  <li><p>
The <em>decomposition group of $\mathfrak m$</em> is the subgroup $D = \{ \sigma \in G \mid \sigma (\mathfrak m) = \mathfrak m\} $. 
</p>
</li><li><p>
The <em>inertia group of $\mathfrak m$</em> is the kernel $I$ of the map $D \to \text{Aut}(\kappa (\mathfrak m)/\kappa _ A)$. 
</p>
</li>
</ol></p>
</article>